#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384ce5b6-40da-59a0-bc87-a1d726328cc2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Finite Area Bounded Between a Curve and the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f742ada-acb5-5e20-9b9d-e2ba3383764f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f742ada-acb5-5e20-9b9d-e2ba3383764f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293426} :answer-field/id #uuid "724754c0-f45b-57b2-9042-56fefca97246" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b02a57a4-6817-5d59-84b9-fa9676c32001" :question/math-academy-id "q-346674" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\le 0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
